   "subject": "Identifying outlying loci",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi Everyone,</div><div>I am trying to identify the outlying loci in my SNP data. I have used gl.outflank(gi, plot=True), which identified 10 loci with High Fst (below). Is there away to get the names of those 10 loci ?</div><div><pre style=\"color:#dedede;font-size:10pt;font-family:Lucida Console;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-transform:none;text-indent:0;background-color:black;white-space:pre-wrap;margin:0;border-width:4px;border-style:none;letter-spacing:normal;word-spacing:0px;line-height:15px;outline:currentcolor none medium;word-break:break-all\"><span><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;margin:0;border-width:4px;border-style:none;word-break:break-all;outline:currentcolor none medium\">$outflank$numberHighFstOutliers\n[1] 10</span></span></pre></div><div>Thanks heaps!</div><div></div><div>Robert<br></div><div><pre style=\"color:#dedede;font-size:10pt;font-family:Lucida Console;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-transform:none;text-indent:0;background-color:black;white-space:pre-wrap;margin:0;border-width:4px;border-style:none;letter-spacing:normal;word-spacing:0px;line-height:15px;outline:currentcolor none medium;word-break:break-all\"><span><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;margin:0;border-width:4px;border-style:none;word-break:break-all;outline:currentcolor none medium\"></span></span></pre></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "_dfb3AtqFwAJ",
