     3,
     "<div lang=\"EN-AU\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\"><div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">From:</span></b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\"> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">da...@googlegroups.com</a> [mailto:<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">da...@googlegroups.com</a>]\r\n<b>On Behalf Of </b>Robert O<br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> Saturday, 2 February 2019 11:52<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> dartR &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">da...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> [dartR] Identifying outlying loci<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Hi Everyone,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I am trying to identify the outlying loci in my SNP data. I have used gl.outflank(gi, plot=True), which identified 10 loci with High Fst (below). Is there away to get the names of those 10 loci ?<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<pre style=\"line-height:11.25pt;background:black;word-break:break-all;white-space:pre-wrap;outline:currentcolor none medium;word-spacing:0px\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:#dedede;border:none windowtext 1.0pt;padding:0cm\">$outflank$numberHighFstOutliers<u></u><u></u></span></pre>\r\n<pre style=\"line-height:11.25pt;background:black;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:#dedede;border:none windowtext 1.0pt;padding:0cm\">[1] 10</span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:#dedede\"><u></u><u></u></span></pre>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Thanks heaps!<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Robert<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div></div>"
